## User request
For embedded files, particularly removals, show the number of items in the map dependent on each file before and after the change. Highlight zero-use embedded assets so users can distinguish unused-file cleanup from removing assets still referenced by placed items.

## Acceptance criteria
- Show clearly labeled before/after usage counts for added, removed and modified embedded files in applicable diff outputs, with structured counts for machine-readable consumers.
- Count placed instances, preserving duplicates, and resolve actual embedded model identities/aliases rather than assuming displayed or compacted path equality.
- Define dependency scope explicitly: direct placed-item references versus transitive asset dependencies. When transitive or unresolved dependencies cannot be established, report unknown/uncertain instead of asserting zero or safe removal.
- Removed embedded files must show whether the new map still contains references to them. Missing file on one side does not imply zero usages on that side.
- Distinguish confirmed zero direct uses from unknown counts; avoid claiming removal is risk-free solely from an incomplete reference scan.
- Tests cover zero-use cleanup, multiple placed instances, alias/path variants, removed-but-still-referenced assets, additions, unchanged usage, and unresolved dependencies.

## Sequencing
Backlog addition requested during the fixed 26-ticket batch; preserve as a separate pending bug, not automatic expansion of that implementation batch.

Decision: implement after B060 in the same worktree because both touch shared diff comparison/report models and renderers; validate B061 against the landed B060 contracts.